install: add SYNC and prove the allocation reached the volume header

Hardware on 2026-10-28 showed the install writing nothing that survived a
REBOOT: skel 16/16 and base 6/6 reported OK with matching INST CHECK
read-backs, then /private/etc/passwd was MISSING and INST? still reported
the pre-install free count.  The writes and their in-memory metadata died
at the reset; even a 64 KiB stream lost 100%.

The stream-end VFS_SYNC from 0148 is the fix for the metadata, but it has
to be observable.  Add:

  - SYNC console command: VFS_SYNC + SYNCHRONIZE CACHE, then read the HFS+
    volume header back from the device and print free before/after/delta.
    Works with kebab_noinit=1 because it does not need the init thread;
  - INST FREE at each stream completion: the volume header's free-block
    count before the stream and after the flush, the delta, and the block
    count expected from the bytes written net of the old contents replaced;
  - INST? vh: the on-disk volume header's free count alongside the mounted
    statfs, without issuing a raw read while a stream is live.

The orchestrator asserts INST FREE: when a stream wrote files, delta must
be positive and at least three quarters of expected.  The fake board gets a
free-stuck injection that reproduces the hardware result, so a clean
INST DONE without free-block movement now fails the run instead of passing
and losing the data at the next reboot.

